@scene(100)

// Debug scene: one wood.whiteOak ball, alone, at a small scene size — isolates
// the cost of a single material.withDisplacement preset (grain-ring
// relief) from everything else in Texture Library.gsl. The displaced
// field's height comes from a real noise function defined over all of
// space, not just near the surface, so the raymarch's gradient-based step
// correction can shrink steps well before the ray ever nears the ball —
// this scene tests whether that alone is enough to be expensive.

oakMat, oakColor = wood.whiteOak([0, 0, -25], [0, 0, 1]);
ball = sphere(25);
ball.material = oakMat;
ball.color = oakColor;

return ball;
